# Tokens & markup (ideal-stack)

**Owns:** project `@theme` token vocabulary and the Canvas Inspector `data-as-*` contract for **project / Live** pages. **Laws** (native tags, no JS layout, dual faces): `architecture/semantic-html-css.mdc` — do not restate.

## Design tokens (project `@theme`)

**Golden sentence:** Visitor HTML ships **semantic token utilities** only. Raw hex / Tailwind gray-zinc-slate palettes / `white/10` opacity hacks = fail ship bar.

| Job | Prefer |
| --- | --- |
| Page canvas | `bg-paper` `text-ink` |
| Raised surface | `bg-paper-raised` |
| Muted band / soft fill | `bg-sand` `text-ink-soft` |
| Borders | `border-line` |
| Brand / accent | `bg-accent` `text-accent` `text-inverse-fg` (on accent) |
| Display type | `font-display` + size utilities |

Map other projects the same way: **name the role in `@theme`**, then use that name in class strings — never paint with `#0f1115`.

### Ship bar

| Score | Styling |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Raw hex/rgb; `bg-zinc-*` / `text-white` / `border-white/10` |
| 1 | `dark:` / `light:` prefixes to fake brand appearance |
| 2 | Opacity-only washes without `color-mix` + token |
| 3 | Mixed semantic + raw |
| **4+** | Semantic utilities only — **minimum to ship** |

### Band model

1. **Section** owns the band (`transparent` / `muted` / `brand` / `surface`) — see `design/layout.mdc`.
2. **Children inherit** ink/soft; don't re-paint the band on Container.
3. **Controls** (Button) bring their own surface via project `className` / `data-variant` — pick contrast for the parent band.
4. **Never** use a flipping inverse band for normal marketing rhythm (`bg-inverse` broke under `.dark`).

### Never

| Don't | Why |
| --- | --- |
| `#fff`, `#0b1220`, `bg-slate-900`, `text-white` | Bypasses `@theme`; breaks light/dark |
| Container `bg-*` with no border/radius | Naked slab — bordered surface rule |
| `attrs.style` / inline `style=` for colors | Use classes + tokens |
| Parallel token language beside `@theme` | One design system per project |

## Tailwind on the semantic tag

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| Utilities on the landmark/control (`section`, `button`, …) | Parallel BEM / big CSS modules for look |
| Project `@theme` token utilities | Raw hex when a token exists |
| Headless primitives take `className` from compose | Bake brand into shared primitive defaults |

## Inspector attribution (`data-as-*`)

Every **design-registry** render (SSR HTML **and** remix/ui) stamps Inspect so Live + DOM reading stay trivial.

| Attr | Required on | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `data-as-inspect="1"` | Component root + slot hosts | opt-in |
| `data-as-kind` | Same | `component` \| `slot` \| `prop` \| `markdown` \| `text` |
| `data-as-component` | Component root + its slots | registry id (`blog-hero`, `button`, `section`) |
| `data-as-slot` | Slot hosts | `title`, `label`, … |
| `data-as-instance` | Live page instances | `home-hero`, `home-cta-primary` |
| `data-as-source` | When bound to a file | `content/pages/home.md` |

Prefer **`stampComponentAttrs` / `stampSlotAttrs`** (`@glassbox-studio/canvas-inspector` or project `inspect-stamp`) over hand-rolled strings.

```html
<section
  class="relative w-full …"
  data-as-inspect="1"
  data-as-kind="component"
  data-as-component="blog-hero"
  data-as-instance="home-hero"
  data-as-source="content/pages/home.md"
>
  <h1 data-as-inspect="1" data-as-kind="slot" data-as-component="blog-hero" data-as-slot="title">…</h1>
</section>
```

**Strip in prod** when `shouldStripAuthoringAttrs` — attrs are authoring-time; semantics + Tailwind stay.

